      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Serum activity of creatine kinase and creatine kinase-MB have been investigated in 129 patients of various etiology in overt heart failure. Elevations in CK-MB were found in 19 patients, most frequently in patients with inflammatory heart disease. We found no correlation between CK-MB activity in serum and the severity of heart failure. CK-MB elevation in patients with chronic heart failure may be interpreted as a sign of progressive as well as regressive processes in the myocardium."},
